{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.HydrogenShellWrithe","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.HydrogenShellWrithe","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:hydrogen_shell_writhe_conditional_on_borromean_quark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"hydrogen_shell_writhe_conditional_on_borromean_quark","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L67-L76","doc":"Witness theorem: this file's proposition is conditional on\n`BorromeanQuark` per CLAUDE.md §3b-cond.  Conditional on the\nBorromean-baryon model, the proton anchor of the electron trefoil\nhas a strictly positive mass scale at the substrate value\n`q = 11/10 > 1` — derived from the class field, not asserted as\n`True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.bareMass_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.bareMass_pos","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L65-L65","doc":"**Conjectural positivity.**  The baryon mass scale is strictly\npositive for every physical `q > 1` (a genuine `q`-quantified\nproperty in the shape of the claim, per §3b-tax). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.bareMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.bareMass","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The bare baryon mass scale (the proton anchor for the electron\ntrefoil), as a function of the substrate parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark","kind":"class","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L53-L65","doc":"Local mirror of `conj:borromean-quark`'s axiomatised class.\nSee `borromean-quark.lean` (canonical declaration, namespace\n`QOU.Archimedean`) for the full content.  The field carries the\ngenuine conjectural content — the positive baryon (proton-anchor)\nmass scale set by the Borromean volume — not a bare `True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.hydrogen_shell_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.hydrogen_shell_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L28-L38","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:hydrogen-shell-writhe","label":"conj:hydrogen-shell-writhe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.orbitalCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.orbitalCount","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L25-L26","doc":"Orbital count at shell n equals n². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.shellFromWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.shellFromWrithe","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/hydrogen-shell-writhe.lean#L21-L23","doc":"Shell-writhe correspondence: n = (w-1)/2 maps writhe to principal quantum number.\nGround state has w = 3 (n = 1), excited states have w = 2n+1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}